## DESCRIPTION
## Lagrange multipliers
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Lagrange multipliers')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserPopUp.pl", "PGchoicemacros.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

@lst = ["?", "Local maximum on C", "Local minimum on C", "Neither"];
$mc1 = PopUp(@lst, "Local maximum on C");
$mc2 = PopUp(@lst, "Local minimum on C");
$mc3 = PopUp(@lst, "Neither");
$mc4 = new_checkbox_multiple_choice();
$mc4 -> qa("", "Point P", "Point Q", "Point S");
$mc4 -> makeLast("Point P", "Point Q", "Point R", "Point S");

BEGIN_PGML


Let [` C \subseteq \mathbb{R}^2 `] be the level set of a real-valued [` C^1 `] map [` g `]. The points [` P,Q,R,S `] are on the curve [` C `].

>>[@ image("e6-local-extrema-contour.png", width=>300) @]*<<

Decide which of these points are local maxima on [` C `], local minima on [` C `], or neither.

P: [_]{$mc2}

Q: [_]{$mc2}

R: [_]{$mc3}

S: [_]{$mc1}

Decide which of these points appear to satisfy the corresponding Lagrange system of equations. [@$mc4 -> print_q()@]*

[@$mc4 -> print_a()@]*
END_PGML

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;
ANS( checkbox_cmp($mc4->correct_ans()) );

ENDDOCUMENT();